.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yume-gui
is the desktop window for YUME clients.
It imports sealed kits, starts and stops each kit's
.BR yume (1),
and shows what the running client reports: its connection, traffic,
local listeners, circuits, proposals of a shorter route, printed lines
and fixed security posture.
It runs as an ordinary user and needs no privilege.
.PP
Its tray icon shows the selected kit's state as a dot on the YUME mark:
green while connected, amber while connecting or waiting, red when the
running client reports a failure and grey when it is not running.
The tray's menu connects or disconnects the kit and shows or hides the
window.
.PP
It talks to a running
.B yume
only through that client's control socket, as
.B docs/protocol/CONTROL_1.md
defines, and runs the
.B yume
program to validate, start and import kits.
It starts
.B yume
as a detached process in its own session, so closing or killing the
window leaves the tunnel running, and it stops
.B yume
with the control protocol's stop request.
Opening the window again finds a running client by its socket.
.PP
A kit is a directory under
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/yume/kits
that holds a
.IR yume.json ,
as
.B yume
.B --import-kit
writes it.
.B yume-gui
starts
.B yume
.B --config
.IR kit /yume.json
.B --control-socket
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/yume/ kit .sock .
A kit with a managed TUN adapter needs privileges that this user process
does not have, so run such a kit as a system service instead.
.PP
The Connect page can rename a stopped kit, moving its directory without
rewriting the configuration or credentials and retaining its selection.
An existing name is never replaced.
Both clients' control sockets are checked before the move; an unanswered
or refused socket prevents it.
A configuration with absolute references into the old kit directory must
use relative kit paths without parent traversal before renaming.
A known client whose socket has closed stays active until its process
ends, including after the stop warning.
.PP
The Posture page states the protection the running client reports: the
YTP/1 composition, the evidence profile its outer layers follow, its
tuning limits and the preset they match.
It offers no switch that weakens a tunnel.
A proposal of a shorter route is accepted only from its review dialog,
for that exact proposal.
Closing the dialog accepts nothing.
