.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--kit " name
Select the kit named
.I name
when the window opens.
With
.B --headless
it names the kit to act on.
.TP
.BI "--page " page
Open the window on
.IR page :
.BR overview ,
.BR connect ,
.B logs
or
.BR posture .
.TP
.BI "--theme " theme
Use
.BR light ,
.B dark
or the desktop's
.B system
theme for this run instead of the one chosen in the window, which is
saved in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/yume/gui.conf .
Light is the default.
.TP
.BI "--layout-direction " direction
Lay the window out
.B ltr
or
.BR rtl ,
mirroring it for right-to-left scripts.
Text in any script is shaped either way.
.TP
.BI "--size " size
Open the window at
.IR size ,
written as width
.B x
height in pixels.
.TP
.B --no-tray
Show no tray icon.
With a tray icon, closing the window hides it and the GUI stays in the
tray, and Quit in the tray's menu ends the GUI.
Without one, closing the window ends the GUI.
A tunnel keeps running either way.
.TP
.BI "--yume " path
Run the
.B yume
program at
.IR path .
Without it,
.B yume-gui
runs the
.B yume
in its own directory and does not search
.BR PATH .
.TP
.BI "--capture " directory
Wait for the selected kit's first status, save each page and the route
review dialog, when a proposal is shown, to
.I directory
as
.IR page - theme - direction .png,
and the tray icon in each state as
.RI tray- state .png,
and exit.
The exit status is 1 when an image could not be written or a page raised
a QML warning.
.TP
.BI "--headless " action
Without a window, act on the kit that
.B --kit
names, as the window's buttons do, and print one JSON line per step with
what the control socket reported.
.B status
asks once.
.B connect
starts the kit and waits up to 60 seconds until
.B yume
reports
.BR connected ,
then exits and leaves the tunnel running.
.B stop
waits until the socket is gone and the process has ended.
.B cycle
connects, stops, connects and stops.
.TP
.BI "--import-kit " file
Import the sealed kit in
.I file
as the kit
.B --name
names, reading its code from standard input, as the Connect page does.
.B yume
.B --import-kit
opens and writes it.
.TP
.BI "--name " name
The kit's name: 1 to 48 letters, digits, dots, dashes or underscores,
not starting with a dot or a dash.
.TP
.B --version
Print the product version, the Qt version in use and the control
protocol.
.TP
.BI "--completion " shell
Print the completion script for
.IR shell ,
which must be
.BR bash ,
and exit.
The script completes this program's options, their fixed values and file
arguments.
To load it for one user, save it as
.IR ~/\:.local/\:share/\:bash-completion/\:completions/\:yume-gui .
This opens no window.
.TP
.B --help
Print a short usage summary.
.SH FILES
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/yume/kits/ name**
is a kit.
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/yume/ name .sock
is its running client's control socket, and
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/yume/ name .log
holds what that client printed since this GUI last started it.
The runtime directory must be set, and
.I yume
in it is kept private to the user.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The window exits with 0.
.B --headless
and
.B --import-kit
exit with 0 when every step passed, 1 when a step failed and 2 when
nothing could be done, such as for an unknown kit or a usage error.
.B --capture
exits with 0 or 1.
.BR --help ,
.B --version
and
.B --completion
exit with 0, and a usage error exits with 2.
